  "reel": {
    "script": "Ever wonder if your dog knows when you're sad or angry? Scientists have long suspected dogs can read our emotions. Now, they've found the proof. Researchers trained 12 dogs to sit still in an fMRI machine. They showed the dogs images of human faces expressing different emotions. The dogs' brains showed distinct activity patterns. Especially for happiness. Dogs can distinguish between human fear and sadness. This study, published in iScience, shows that dogs process smiles in a unique brain region. It also shows they can tell the difference between negative emotions. This research deepens our understanding of the human-canine bond. It highlights the incredible emotional intelligence of our furry friends. It's a reminder of how connected we are to our pets. And how much they truly understand us. Do you think your dog knows when you're happy or sad? Share your stories below!",
