    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "Ever wonder if your dog knows when you're sad or angry?"
      },
      {
        "text": "Scientists have long suspected dogs can read our emotions."
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, they've found the proof."
      },
      {
        "text": "Researchers trained 12 dogs to sit still in an fMRI machine."
      },
      {
        "text": "They showed the dogs images of human faces expressing different emotions."
      },
      {
        "text": "The dogs' brains showed distinct activity patterns."
      },
      {
        "text": "Especially for happiness."
      },
      {
        "text": "Dogs can distinguish between human fear and sadness."
      },
      {
        "text": "This study, published in iScience, shows that dogs process smiles in a unique brain region."
      },
      {
        "text": "It also shows they can tell the difference between negative emotions."
      },
      {
        "text": "This research deepens our understanding of the human-canine bond."
      },
      {
        "text": "It highlights the incredible emotional intelligence of our furry friends."
      },
      {
        "text": "It's a reminder of how connected we are to our pets."
      },
      {
        "text": "And how much they truly understand us."
      },
      {
        "text": "Do you think your dog knows when you're happy or sad?"
      },
      {
        "text": "Share your stories below!"
      }
